cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use cma-mcp in academic, applied, or compliance work,
  please cite it using the metadata below.
title: "cma-mcp: Model Context Protocol distribution for the compound practice loop"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lucic
    given-names: Lovro
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9976-6933"
    website: "https://blog.clarethium.com"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/cma-mcp/"
abstract: >-
  cma-mcp is the Model Context Protocol server that exposes the cma
  compound practice loop to any MCP-compatible AI client (Claude
  Desktop, Cursor, Cline, Continue.dev, and others). The server is a
  thin distribution wrapper around the canonical cma reference
  implementation, the command-line tool it invokes as a subprocess.
  cma-mcp's contribution is reach: bringing the same
  capture-and-surface discipline to environments where the
  cma CLI's shell hooks do not run.
keywords:
  - mcp
  - model-context-protocol
  - compound-practice
  - failure-capture
  - decision-tracking
  - prevention
  - cma
  - clarethium
license: Apache-2.0
